  "raw_text": "Step 1: To find the angle $\\angle ABC$, we can use the dot product formula between vectors $\\overrightarrow{BA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{BC}$. The formula for the cosine of the angle between two vectors is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC}}{|\\overrightarrow{BA}| |\\overrightarrow{BC}|}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: First, calculate vector $\\overrightarrow{BA}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BA} = A - B = (1-3, -11+4, 2-1) = (-2, -7, 1)\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Next, calculate vector $\\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BC} = C - B = (-2-3, 1+4, -1-1) = (-5, 5, -2)\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate the dot product $\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{BA} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{BC} = (-2)(-5) + (-7)(5) + (1)(-2) = 10 - 35 - 2 = -27\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Calculate the magnitude of $\\overrightarrow{BA}$:\n\\[\n|\\overrightarrow{BA}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-7)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 1} = \\sqrt{54}\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Calculate the magnitude of $\\overrightarrow{BC}$:\n\\[\n|\\overrightarrow{BC}| = \\sqrt{(-5)^2 + 5^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 25 + 4} = \\sqrt{54}\n\\]\n\nStep 7: Substitute these values into the cosine formula to find $\\cos(\\theta)$:\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{-27}{\\sqrt{54} \\cdot \\sqrt{54}} = \\frac{-27}{54} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Find the angle $\\theta$ using the inverse cosine function:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\nStep 9: Convert the angle from radians to degrees:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\approx 120^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{120}<|im_end|>",
