    "solution": "From the distance formula, we compute that $AB = 3 \\sqrt{6},$ $AC = 9 \\sqrt{2},$ and $BC = 3 \\sqrt{6}.$  Then from the Law of Cosines,\n\\[\\cos \\angle ABC = \\frac{(3 \\sqrt{6})^2 + (3 \\sqrt{6})^2 - (9 \\sqrt{2})^2}{2 \\cdot 3 \\sqrt{6} \\cdot 3 \\sqrt{6}} = -\\frac{1}{2}.\\]Therefore, $\\angle ABC = \\boxed{120^\\circ}.$",
